    "title": "Banana Ball World Tour coming to Myrtle Beach in 2027 at Pelicans Ballpark - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kyle St. Clair ,\n2 hours ago\nMYRTLE BEACH, S.C. (WBTW) — The Banana Ball World Tour is coming to Myrtle Beach next year for a three-day event at Pelicans Ballpark.\nThe Myrtle Beach Pelicans announced Thursday that the Loco Beach Coconuts will face the Indianapolis Clowns March 18-20, 2027, marking the tour’s first visit to the stadium.\nThe Banana Ball World Tour features the Savannah Bananas and other teams playing a modified version of baseball with unique rules, including fans being able to record outs by catching foul balls.\nFans interested in attending must sign up for the ticket lottery by Oct. 31.\n* * *\nKyle St. Clair is a Digital Producer at News13. He is from Warrenton, Virginia, and joined the News13 team in July 2026. He graduated cum laude from Coastal Carolina University in May 2026. Follow Kyle on Facebook , X , Instagram , and read more of his work here .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WBTW.",
    "summary": "By Kyle St. Clair , MYRTLE BEACH, S.C. (WBTW) — The Banana Ball World Tour is coming to Myrtle Beach next year for a three-day event at Pelicans Ballpark. The Myrtle Beach Pelicans announced Thursday that the Loco Beach Coconuts will face the Indianapolis Clowns March 18-20, 2027, marking the tour’s first visit to the stadium. The Banana Ball World Tour features the Savannah Bananas and other teams playing a modified version of baseball with unique rules, including fans being able to record outs by catching foul balls.",
